The more threads that exist, the more time the CPU spends performing context switches instead of executing useful work.

Memory Usage

Every thread has its own stack.

10000 Threads

↓

10000 Stacks

As the number of connections increases, memory consumption also increases significantly.

Thread Pool

Instead of creating one thread for every client, the server creates a fixed number of worker threads when it starts.

For example,

8 Worker Threads

These workers are reused for every new client connection.

