Key Takeaway

A thread pool does not eliminate waiting.

It simply moves waiting from expensive threads to a lightweight queue, resulting in:

Lower memory usage.
Fewer context switches.
Reusable worker threads.
More predictable resource consumption.

The work still gets done, but the server uses system resources much more efficiently.